# Empirical resolution-order study (gcc 16, Fedora, 2026-10-14)
# Marker headers: const char* sluice_f10_<name>_marker in each dir.

== which liburing.h a C++ compile opens ==
C_INCLUDE_PATH only      => (ignored: no marker, falls through to system header)
CPATH only               => cpath marker
CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH only  => cplus marker
CPATH+CPLUS              => cpath marker

== g++ -E -xc++ -v search list with CPATH+cplus set ==
 /tmp/f10-study/cpath-dir
 /tmp/f10-study/cplus-dir
 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-redhat-linux/16/../../../../include/c++/16
 ... (backward, gcc internal, /usr/local/include, /usr/include)

== -I vs CPATH (both present) ==
g++ -c -I stub-good -o o.cpp with CPATH=stub-bad => stub-bad wins (env paths rank ahead of -I)

== linker -Wl,--trace ==
default:                  /usr/lib/gcc/.../lib64/liburing.so (configured dirs)
LIBRARY_PATH=fakelib:     still configured dirs (LIBRARY_PATH checked last)
-L fakelib:               fakelib/liburing.so (-L beats configured dirs)
